WEBVTT

00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:39.849
Just so you know,

00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:43.186
none of us are dropping out.

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:45.313
We...

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:48.274
...will win.

00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:57.992
Fir st string, welcome back
from your tour abroad.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:01.913
There are some people here who
don't seem to know their place.

00:02:03.331 --> 00:02:05.750
Are you guys behind this?

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.670
This is merely an annual event.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.883
You haven't changed.

00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:14.509
Oh?

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.429
I don't recognize him.

00:02:17.762 --> 00:02:20.140
We picked him up overseas.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.852
He's good. And he's a Japanese citizen.

00:02:26.938 --> 00:02:32.944
"The Battle Begins"

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:36.698
Sadaharu, let me handle this.

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.367
Black Revolutionary Brigade jerseys, huh?

00:02:39.784 --> 00:02:42.120
So you came here to beat us?

00:02:42.454 --> 00:02:46.374
Then, if you manage to defeat me,

00:02:46.374 --> 00:02:49.044
I'll give you this national team pin.

00:02:49.336 --> 00:02:53.673
So if you play us, you won't
show any mercy, then?

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:57.844
Actually, I'm glad I got to
see you at this camp.

00:02:59.137 --> 00:03:01.931
It's been a while, Akuto-<i>niisan</i>.

00:03:03.266 --> 00:03:05.185
You know him, Renji?

00:03:05.977 --> 00:03:07.395
Then I won't--

00:03:07.395 --> 00:03:09.814
"Then I won't hold back."

00:03:10.815 --> 00:03:13.860
That's what you're going to say.

00:03:19.449 --> 00:03:23.078
Probability of a cross: 73%.

00:03:24.913 --> 00:03:30.502
But probabilities change based
on the factors you predict.

00:03:31.753 --> 00:03:36.675
Probability I'll go for a Passing Shot: 78%.

00:03:38.176 --> 00:03:39.219
No problem.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:44.432
Renji already knows what's coming next.

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:47.185
An irregular bounce?

00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:50.939
U-17 training camp.

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:55.860
Strengthening Court 36,
inside west side sideline.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.654
11:00, clear skies.

00:03:57.654 --> 00:04:02.784
The chance of an irregular bounce under
normal conditions is a mere 2.1%.

00:04:03.201 --> 00:04:08.707
Probability Renji Yanagi isn't
prepared for an irregular bounce...

00:04:10.458 --> 00:04:12.335
90%.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.673
He's using Data Tennis, too?

00:04:21.344 --> 00:04:25.098
Based on the data thus far,
his next return will be...

00:04:35.316 --> 00:04:36.609
What is this?

00:04:40.655 --> 00:04:43.158
Something's wrong with Renji.

00:05:15.899 --> 00:05:16.524
Renji!

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:19.569
Why didn't you return that shot?

00:05:19.569 --> 00:05:20.570
It's checkmate.

00:05:22.197 --> 00:05:26.159
Renji Yanagi has seen the end of this match.

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:27.619
Renji...

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.583
My odds of winning

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.960
are 0%.

00:05:36.378 --> 00:05:41.966
0%? Is his Data Tennis better than yours?

00:05:42.884 --> 00:05:45.303
It's not at all surprising.

00:05:45.887 --> 00:05:47.931
I taught Renji

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:51.976
only a little bit of my Data Tennis.

00:05:52.435 --> 00:05:53.853
Taught him?

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:54.646
Yes.

00:05:55.313 --> 00:05:59.401
I learned Data Tennis from Akuto-niisan.

00:06:00.652 --> 00:06:01.611
Sadaharu,

00:06:02.487 --> 00:06:04.906
it was before you and I met.

00:06:06.533 --> 00:06:08.326
A chance meeting

00:06:08.326 --> 00:06:10.995
changed my tennis career.

00:06:17.002 --> 00:06:18.837
What was that?

00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:20.714
Data Tennis.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.384
Data Tennis...

00:06:25.635 --> 00:06:30.515
By gathering and analyzing
all data and information,

00:06:30.515 --> 00:06:33.101
I could predict future events.

00:06:33.101 --> 00:06:37.063
It was the style I'd been looking for.

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:40.567
Everything is made up of information.

00:06:40.567 --> 00:06:43.528
When that information becomes yours,

00:06:43.528 --> 00:06:45.739
it becomes tremendous power.

00:06:46.114 --> 00:06:48.700
Wow! That's amazing, Akuto-niisan!

00:06:50.035 --> 00:06:53.580
Information can be used as a weapon, Renji.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:58.918
I was drawn to Data Tennis and
decided to master it myself.

00:07:02.005 --> 00:07:05.425
But my Data Tennis isn't good enough...

00:07:06.718 --> 00:07:08.386
...to beat me.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:18.521
Did you know?

00:07:19.647 --> 00:07:23.443
It's only the strong that
get to stand on the court.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.700
Y-You guys are...

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.869
The middle school losers?

00:07:34.412 --> 00:07:34.996
Ten points.

00:07:35.246 --> 00:07:35.914
Ten points.

00:07:36.206 --> 00:07:36.998
Ten points.

00:07:36.998 --> 00:07:39.918
Thirty points total for Momoshiro!

00:07:39.918 --> 00:07:40.710
Wait, what the hell?

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.170
Huh?

00:07:42.545 --> 00:07:44.422
Kenya, it's been a while.

00:07:44.422 --> 00:07:47.425
You've grown a lot since I last saw you.

00:07:47.425 --> 00:07:51.680
Yeah. Back then, we had
to change your diapers.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.808
Yeah, that's right. I could barely walk yet.

00:07:54.808 --> 00:07:57.977
Wait, what the hell?! You never
changed my diapers, moron!

00:07:57.977 --> 00:07:59.104
Moron?

00:07:59.104 --> 00:08:00.772
Who's a moron?

00:08:01.231 --> 00:08:04.901
Uh, Kenya-<i>san</i>, do you know those guys?

00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:05.985
I'm confused...

00:08:06.611 --> 00:08:07.737
Yeah.

00:08:07.737 --> 00:08:10.490
This is Hirazen and Haratetsu.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.785
Legendary former captains
of the Shitenhoji tennis team.

00:08:13.785 --> 00:08:16.538
Shitenhoji's legendary captains?

00:08:16.538 --> 00:08:17.414
Yeah.

00:08:17.956 --> 00:08:21.126
That's the "Retort Vending Machine" Haratetsu,

00:08:21.126 --> 00:08:25.213
or Tetsuya Hara-<i>san</i>, whom Shiraishi
took over for last spring.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:28.508
What the hell? Who says? What's your deal?

00:08:30.427 --> 00:08:34.222
And that's the "Laughing Hitman" Hirazen,

00:08:34.222 --> 00:08:37.934
or Yoshiyuki Taira-<i>san</i>,
who captained when we were first years.

00:08:38.518 --> 00:08:42.147
Who's the "Laughing Hitman"?

00:08:42.147 --> 00:08:44.482
I am.

00:08:45.108 --> 00:08:46.568
Hey, Kenya,

00:08:46.568 --> 00:08:51.406
doesn't this remind you
of the first time we met?

00:08:51.406 --> 00:08:52.782
Yeah.

00:08:52.782 --> 00:08:56.286
You taught me about comedy.

00:08:59.122 --> 00:09:02.834
It was the day I first met Haratetsu-<i>san</i>...

00:09:06.004 --> 00:09:07.547
Wait, why are we back here?

00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:09.758
I thought a flashback was starting.

00:09:10.258 --> 00:09:12.510
Sorry. I don't remember.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:16.806
A situation like this should lead to
a story about an inspiring meeting.

00:09:16.806 --> 00:09:21.561
Then it's, "So this guy's comedy
spirit comes from his senpai?"

00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:25.523
And finally, you end with a big laugh.

00:09:25.857 --> 00:09:28.026
But there was no inspiring meeting.

00:09:28.026 --> 00:09:30.779
And I didn't learn about comedy from you.

00:09:31.154 --> 00:09:34.491
You're supposed to be tactful and make
up something appropriate, idiot!

00:09:34.491 --> 00:09:37.243
Explosive response and speed
are critical to comedy!

00:09:37.494 --> 00:09:39.829
No one's faster than me.

00:09:39.829 --> 00:09:40.914
After all, I'm--

00:09:41.331 --> 00:09:43.249
Naniwa's Steam Sauna, right?

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:45.627
That's right. Let's do some deep sweating.

00:09:45.627 --> 00:09:46.961
Wait, what the hell?!

00:09:46.961 --> 00:09:48.171
--So, a what sauna?
--Uh...

00:09:48.171 --> 00:09:48.963
--Not just a sauna. A speed sauna.
--Uh...

00:09:48.963 --> 00:09:50.256
--Not just a sauna. A speed sauna.
--What am I doing here, again?

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:52.217
--But a speed sauna's just fast.
--What am I doing here, again?

00:09:52.217 --> 00:09:54.344
--What's wrong with that?
--Excuse me...

00:09:54.344 --> 00:09:58.014
Can we go to the first aid office now?

00:09:58.014 --> 00:09:59.557
You're still here?!

00:09:59.557 --> 00:10:02.268
Sorry, I forgot.

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:05.605
Go ahead. We'll handle this.

00:10:06.898 --> 00:10:07.816
Oh?

00:10:08.775 --> 00:10:12.904
You guys really want to play us?

00:10:14.864 --> 00:10:16.074
Impossible.

00:10:16.074 --> 00:10:19.911
Mitsuya may have taught you Data Tennis,

00:10:20.203 --> 00:10:25.000
but you can't possibly see the
outcome of the match this early on.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:30.088
All the information came
flooding into my head.

00:10:30.964 --> 00:10:33.216
All the answers were there.

00:10:33.967 --> 00:10:36.886
Nothing I do now will mean anything.

00:10:38.304 --> 00:10:40.473
The outcome won't change.

00:10:41.808 --> 00:10:43.727
That's right, Renji!

00:10:45.353 --> 00:10:50.817
Normally, Data Tennis predicts
the probability of future events

00:10:50.817 --> 00:10:53.570
by gathering as much information as possible.

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:57.699
But that's not all Data Tennis can do.

00:11:01.911 --> 00:11:02.704
"Collecting."

00:11:03.747 --> 00:11:06.666
Data isn't just input.

00:11:06.666 --> 00:11:09.627
It can be output, as well.

00:11:11.463 --> 00:11:13.798
When you strike the ball with the racket,

00:11:13.798 --> 00:11:18.178
"speed," "the ball's path,"
"degree of ball deformation,"

00:11:18.178 --> 00:11:21.181
"angle of the ball's rotation axis,"
"rotational speed,"

00:11:21.181 --> 00:11:25.268
and "frictional heat generated by
the air and minuscule particles,"

00:11:25.268 --> 00:11:29.564
as well as "your opponent's potential"
and "the court's condition"

00:11:29.564 --> 00:11:35.820
and other factors all intertwine, diverge,
and produce countless "outcomes."

00:11:37.572 --> 00:11:42.202
And Data Tennis determines
the most probable outcome!

00:11:42.577 --> 00:11:43.828
You're wrong.

00:11:43.828 --> 00:11:46.414
That's only a part of Data Tennis.

00:11:46.414 --> 00:11:47.499
What?

00:11:47.499 --> 00:11:53.338
My Data Tennis can confront my opponent
with every possible "outcome."

00:11:53.338 --> 00:11:55.632
Confront them?

00:11:55.924 --> 00:11:57.300
I told you.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:01.262
Data isn't just input.
It can be output, as well.

00:12:01.638 --> 00:12:02.305
In other words...

00:12:03.723 --> 00:12:08.937
I can forcefully send data into
my opponent's consciousness.

00:12:09.521 --> 00:12:13.692
Every possible "outcome,"
a tremendous amount of data.

00:12:13.692 --> 00:12:17.278
When that data exceeds the maximum
amount he can process, it eventually...

00:12:21.199 --> 00:12:25.453
You blast your opponents with an
overwhelming torrent of data,

00:12:25.453 --> 00:12:26.913
until it swallows them...

00:12:28.456 --> 00:12:30.166
...and paralyzes them.

00:12:30.166 --> 00:12:33.586
It's an anti-Data Tennis technique. It's...

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:36.047
An "information attack"!

00:12:37.507 --> 00:12:39.217
I told you before.

00:12:39.634 --> 00:12:42.387
Information can be used as a weapon,

00:12:42.387 --> 00:12:43.263
Renji.

00:12:52.939 --> 00:12:53.982
Kenya-<i>san</i>.

00:12:53.982 --> 00:12:54.607
What?

00:12:54.941 --> 00:12:57.736
Why is his nickname Haratetsu?

00:13:00.363 --> 00:13:03.616
Because his name's Tetsuya Hara-<i>san</i>.

00:13:03.616 --> 00:13:04.868
No, no!

00:13:05.118 --> 00:13:08.288
It's because I've got a picture of
Tetsu Ishida on my stomach <i>(hara)</i>!

00:13:08.288 --> 00:13:11.583
That's not Tetsu, it's Gin!
That makes you Haragin!

00:13:16.046 --> 00:13:17.339
Kapow!

00:13:19.132 --> 00:13:19.883
Crap!

00:13:20.216 --> 00:13:21.301
Okay!

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:23.219
You're not getting past me!

00:13:25.847 --> 00:13:28.308
Whoa, he just broke Momoshiro's strings...

00:13:34.272 --> 00:13:35.690
Seriously?

00:13:43.073 --> 00:13:47.369
That's him... Shitenhoji's Laughing Hitman.

00:13:48.495 --> 00:13:51.956
His comedy and shots are both non-standard!

00:14:00.632 --> 00:14:03.551
Have you really given up, Renji?

00:14:05.261 --> 00:14:06.888
That's right.

00:14:06.888 --> 00:14:11.559
All you can do is gather and analyze data.

00:14:12.227 --> 00:14:16.481
You can't fight the conclusion drawn from it.

00:14:20.026 --> 00:14:20.694
No...

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:23.446
He's wrong.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:31.788
My conclusion that I have
0% chance of winning...

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:36.668
This conclusion flushed
all the hope from my body.

00:14:37.669 --> 00:14:39.254
That's exactly right.

00:14:39.254 --> 00:14:41.506
You have no hope left.

00:14:42.924 --> 00:14:46.678
Then why don't you stop attacking?

00:14:48.054 --> 00:14:52.851
There should be no need to continue
blasting this torrent of data at me.

00:14:54.102 --> 00:14:58.231
It's because you're still standing there.

00:14:59.774 --> 00:15:03.111
Despite facing overwhelming waves of data,

00:15:03.111 --> 00:15:05.363
you won't move.

00:15:05.363 --> 00:15:08.158
You understand your chance of winning is 0%,

00:15:08.158 --> 00:15:11.619
but you're still looking for a possibility
somewhere inside you.

00:15:11.619 --> 00:15:12.871
Possibility?

00:15:14.205 --> 00:15:16.875
It's futile resistance.

00:15:16.875 --> 00:15:18.501
It's not like you.

00:15:20.337 --> 00:15:22.088
Possibility...

00:15:26.551 --> 00:15:28.678
It's good to be back in this huge bath!

00:15:28.678 --> 00:15:30.388
I feel great!

00:15:31.723 --> 00:15:33.141
Yanagi-<i>senpai</i>!

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:35.185
Akaya.

00:15:35.185 --> 00:15:36.686
Senpai, I...

00:15:36.686 --> 00:15:38.396
Seiichi told me.

00:15:39.147 --> 00:15:41.775
You broke new ground.

00:15:42.484 --> 00:15:44.110
Thank you.

00:15:44.778 --> 00:15:45.820
What's wrong?

00:15:46.196 --> 00:15:49.032
I did nothing to deserve your gratitude.

00:15:49.032 --> 00:15:50.742
No, at that moment...

00:15:57.749 --> 00:16:01.586
Referee, I, Renji Yanagi,
forfeit the match.

00:16:03.838 --> 00:16:05.674
Don't be ridiculous!

00:16:05.674 --> 00:16:07.509
I'm just getting started!

00:16:07.509 --> 00:16:09.427
That's right.
You're just getting started.

00:16:11.471 --> 00:16:15.266
You will be the one
to remain at this camp.

00:16:17.519 --> 00:16:20.855
If you hadn't let me win,

00:16:20.855 --> 00:16:22.399
I wouldn't have been able to move forward.

00:16:23.525 --> 00:16:27.946
You gave me that possibility!

00:16:30.156 --> 00:16:32.283
Possibility, huh?

00:16:39.708 --> 00:16:40.375
Renji!

00:16:55.473 --> 00:16:58.059
Why are you hitting cross court?

00:16:59.269 --> 00:17:02.230
You don't disappoint! You've got
a retort ready for all my moves!

00:17:02.939 --> 00:17:05.150
Is that something to be impressed by?

00:17:06.818 --> 00:17:09.362
You can't lob the ball there!

00:17:09.696 --> 00:17:12.365
I love hitting smashes!

00:17:12.365 --> 00:17:14.075
Ow!

00:17:14.325 --> 00:17:15.243
Kenya-<i>san</i>!

00:17:15.618 --> 00:17:17.328
You have a bruise on your butt!

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:22.792
H-He took Tetsuya's "Tiger's Meal"
and only got a bruise from it?

00:17:23.209 --> 00:17:25.170
What the hell? What's your deal?

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:27.756
Don't give my moves names!

00:17:31.885 --> 00:17:34.554
I'll blow a hole through your hearts.

00:17:35.555 --> 00:17:39.017
The Hitman's "Kapow" is coming!

00:17:39.017 --> 00:17:40.894
Kapow!

00:17:42.771 --> 00:17:43.355
Momoshiro!

00:17:44.981 --> 00:17:46.941
What are you doing, Momoshiro?

00:17:47.317 --> 00:17:50.236
He'll just break your strings again!

00:17:50.737 --> 00:17:52.697
You can't touch his Kapow!

00:18:00.205 --> 00:18:03.875
Work your way up, Takeshi Momoshiro!

00:18:06.002 --> 00:18:08.630
I won't run! Never!

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:14.469
Captain Hirazen, is that...

00:18:17.097 --> 00:18:20.308
You're probably right.

00:18:20.558 --> 00:18:23.103
Black Jack Knife!

00:18:34.948 --> 00:18:37.992
Let's work our way up, Kenya-<i>san</i>.

00:18:40.745 --> 00:18:42.622
Better believe we will.

00:18:50.588 --> 00:18:51.715
Renji?

00:18:52.674 --> 00:18:54.801
You've abandoned Data Tennis?

00:18:54.801 --> 00:18:56.720
How unsightly, Renji!

00:19:00.598 --> 00:19:02.600
Renji's abandoned Data Tennis?

00:19:03.018 --> 00:19:04.978
No, that's not it.

00:19:04.978 --> 00:19:08.231
I once abandoned data against Renji.

00:19:08.982 --> 00:19:10.025
Could it be...

00:19:18.908 --> 00:19:19.743
Well, well.

00:19:20.285 --> 00:19:23.455
You've gotten pretty good, Kenya.

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:26.875
Thank you.

00:19:27.334 --> 00:19:30.503
Momoshiro, you're pretty impressive, too.

00:19:30.837 --> 00:19:31.921
Thanks!

00:19:31.921 --> 00:19:34.382
A promise is a promise.

00:19:35.216 --> 00:19:37.469
These pins are for you.

00:19:37.761 --> 00:19:39.346
Yeah!

00:19:40.013 --> 00:19:44.768
But only if you can make us laugh with a joke.

00:19:44.768 --> 00:19:47.228
What?!

00:19:56.488 --> 00:19:57.530
Renji.

00:20:02.577 --> 00:20:04.913
Not yet. I'm not...

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:06.915
It's over, Renji.

00:20:06.915 --> 00:20:10.543
No, perhaps I should say it ended long ago.

00:20:10.543 --> 00:20:11.419
I...

00:20:11.419 --> 00:20:13.922
You should have known.

00:20:13.922 --> 00:20:16.132
When you abandoned Data Tennis...

00:20:17.842 --> 00:20:19.386
You died.

00:20:31.523 --> 00:20:32.732
You're wrong.

00:20:33.608 --> 00:20:36.653
Renji didn't abandon Data Tennis.

00:20:36.653 --> 00:20:37.529
What?

00:20:38.113 --> 00:20:42.033
Renji was sending data during the match.

00:20:42.033 --> 00:20:43.827
That's odd.

00:20:43.827 --> 00:20:46.996
I didn't receive anything.

00:20:48.289 --> 00:20:50.709
It seems to have reached you.

00:20:51.668 --> 00:20:52.252
Yes.

00:20:52.836 --> 00:20:54.963
Thanks to the data you sent me,

00:20:54.963 --> 00:20:58.758
my Data Tennis was upgraded.

00:20:59.968 --> 00:21:07.058
Sadaharu, I feel relieved
after that rigorous match...

00:21:08.268 --> 00:21:12.313
I have received all of your "possibilities."

00:21:12.313 --> 00:21:14.899
Leave the rest to me, Renji.

00:21:19.029 --> 00:21:21.531
So you'll take his place?

00:21:22.574 --> 00:21:23.783
Very well.

00:21:23.783 --> 00:21:25.160
I'll play you.

00:21:27.495 --> 00:21:29.456
What's your name?

00:21:30.957 --> 00:21:35.420
Seishun Academy tennis team
third year, Sadaharu Inui.

00:21:36.546 --> 00:21:39.299
I'll grant you a handicap.

00:21:41.259 --> 00:21:46.681
After all, the price you'll pay playing
against us will be unfathomable.

00:23:18.398 --> 00:23:19.441
"Next Time"

00:23:19.441 --> 00:23:21.901
"Next Time"
I have to play a middle schooler?
You must not think much of me.

00:23:21.901 --> 00:23:23.361
I have to play a middle schooler?
You must not think much of me.

00:23:23.361 --> 00:23:25.030
I should say the same thing.

00:23:25.030 --> 00:23:28.908
You're strong, but you're
still only a middle schooler.

00:23:29.367 --> 00:23:30.952
I'll grant you a handicap.

00:23:30.952 --> 00:23:32.162
Really?

00:23:32.162 --> 00:23:34.789
If you don't need to see the ball,

00:23:34.789 --> 00:23:37.709
then I'll take away your sense of sight.

00:23:41.504 --> 00:23:43.590
"Reflection and Illusion"
The next episode of <i>New Prince of</i>
<i>Tennis </i>is: "Reflection and Illusion."

00:23:43.590 --> 00:23:48.480
"Reflection and Illusion"
Perhaps you'd like me to
take your other senses, too.
